.TH TRYX-PANORAMA-MANAGER 1 "2026-08-26" "TRYX Panorama Manager 2.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tryx-panorama-manager \- control compatible TRYX cooler displays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tryx-panorama-manager
.br
.B tryx-panorama-manager
.B \-\-version
.br
.B tryx-panorama-manager
.B \-\-autostart
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TRYX Panorama Manager
is a Qt 6 Quick application for controlling compatible TRYX Panorama,
Panorama SE, and Turris 620 cooler displays on Linux.
The desktop GUI communicates over the user D-Bus session with a separately
packaged private runtime that owns USB, legacy serial/ADB, media, live-metrics,
and firmware operations.
The application uses model-specific media profiles and enables only the
printer-class USB capabilities supported by each device, without bundling
vendor media.
.PP
Starting the graphical application starts the packaged systemd user service on
demand.
The service is installed disabled and is not enabled automatically by the
package.
GUI login startup is separately opt-in through Settings and uses a managed XDG
Autostart entry in the current user's configuration. It never changes the
background runtime service. An autostart launch remains hidden only when Hide
to tray is selected and a StatusNotifier host is available; otherwise the
window is shown.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version and exit without starting the graphical
application or accessing USB.
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Start in login mode. Hide the initial window only when the saved close policy
is Hide to tray and a StatusNotifier host is available. This option does not
enable or disable either GUI autostart or the background runtime service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/tryx-panorama-manager
Qt Quick desktop GUI.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/tryx-panorama-manager/tryx-panorama-runtime
Private background runtime.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/tryx-panorama.service
Systemd user unit for the background runtime.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user-preset/90-tryx-panorama.preset
Preset that keeps the user unit disabled after package installation.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/tryx-panorama-manager.desktop
Optional owner-managed GUI autostart entry created by Settings. If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, the path is
.IR ~/.config/autostart/tryx-panorama-manager.desktop .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-tryx-pase-access.rules
Early supported-device access rule.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-tryx-pase-printer.rules
Late rule that prevents printer-service activation for supported interfaces.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/DXVSI/Tryx-Linux-GUI/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
